WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.305
Lesson 3.5.

00:00:02.305 --> 00:00:05.060
Perpetual futures and margin on-chain.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.440
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.592
able to understand perp positions well enough to

00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:13.359
use them for hedging (Module 11) and carry

00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:16.125
(10.3), and to see why high leverage fails.

00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:18.715
Here's the plan.

00:00:18.715 --> 00:00:20.400
First, the key ideas.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.115
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:24.640
Then, your checklist.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.802
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:30.694
First, A perpetual future (perp) tracks

00:00:30.694 --> 00:00:33.067
an asset's price with no expiry.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.612
You post margin and choose leverage.

00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:38.345
Next, Isolated margin: only the margin

00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:40.607
in that position is at risk.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:43.895
Cross margin: your whole account backs every position

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:46.326
(one bad trade can drain the rest).

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:49.028
Then, Mark price (used for liquidation)

00:00:49.028 --> 00:00:51.490
vs index price (spot reference).

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.258
Funding is paid between longs and shorts,

00:00:54.258 --> 00:00:56.535
usually every hour or 8 hours.

00:00:56.535 --> 00:00:59.044
And finally, Liquidation happens when your

00:00:59.044 --> 00:01:01.620
margin falls to the maintenance margin.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.122
Roughly, a long is liquidated after a fall

00:01:05.122 --> 00:01:08.135
of 1 ÷ leverage − maintenance margin.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.950
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:18.075
Long ETH from $3,000 at 5×, 0.5% maintenance

00:01:18.075 --> 00:01:26.405
margin: the calculator gives liquidation ≈ $2,415 (−19.5%).

00:01:26.405 --> 00:01:30.768
The same short at 20× is liquidated

00:01:30.768 --> 00:01:34.646
at ≈ $3,135 (+4.5%), a move ETH

00:01:34.646 --> 00:01:37.370
can make in an hour.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.189
Leverage doesn't just magnify gains: it shrinks

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:42.010
how wrong you're allowed to be.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.770
Here's your checklist.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.305
Do it now, for real.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:49.020
First, Isolated margin by default.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.280
Next, Liquidation price computed before opening.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.067
Then, Leverage ≤ 2–3× for anything

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.835
but a hedge I fully understand.

00:01:57.835 --> 00:01:59.821
And finally, Funding cost checked

00:01:59.821 --> 00:02:01.165
for how long I'll hold.

00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:03.675
Question 1.

00:02:03.675 --> 00:02:05.685
Isolated vs cross margin?

00:02:10.105 --> 00:02:13.826
The answer: Isolated risks only that position's margin;

00:02:13.826 --> 00:02:17.215
cross puts the whole account behind every position.

00:02:18.515 --> 00:02:19.760
Question 2.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.884
Roughly how far can a 10×

00:02:21.884 --> 00:02:25.804
long fall before liquidation (0.5% maintenance)?

00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:32.739
The answer: About 9.5%.

00:02:34.039 --> 00:02:35.309
Question 3.

00:02:35.309 --> 00:02:37.074
Which price triggers liquidation?

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.129
The answer: The mark price.

00:02:44.429 --> 00:02:45.674
Let's recap.

00:02:45.674 --> 00:02:47.945
A perpetual future (perp) tracks an

00:02:47.945 --> 00:02:50.074
asset's price with no expiry.

00:02:50.074 --> 00:02:52.538
Isolated margin: only the margin in

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.549
that position is at risk.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:56.865
Mark price (used for liquidation)

00:02:56.865 --> 00:02:59.344
vs index price (spot reference).

00:02:59.344 --> 00:03:01.443
Liquidation happens when your margin

00:03:01.443 --> 00:03:03.259
falls to the maintenance margin.

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:07.074
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:07.074 --> 00:03:10.846
Next up, Lesson 3.6: Lending design deep dive:

00:03:10.846 --> 00:03:14.939
e-mode, caps, auctions, soft liquidation, bad debt.
